From 17545b8f0626e45526fa4c87e7e7ff34731fe8b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:59:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0164: shop probe at the confirm branch (ItemName field trace)

Static tracing cannot resolve the ItemName field offset: the
0x50a5c0/x22 route ends in a UI-layer item-data object whose
typeinfos are runtime-constructed in BSS, the UI object's +0x150
is an animation name (proved), and ItemName lives in the BYML
layer, read by hash. One logging cut at the router confirm branch
0x442664 dumps the shop structure at confirm time (x19, list,
list+0x20, A = vtable[0](list+0x20), x22 = 0x50a5c0(list+0x20),
0x80 bytes of A and x22, 0x100 bytes of the shop sub-object,
0x200 bytes of the list object) into the probe buffer at state
+0x3300; the host drains it into [shop] log lines once per present.
Object B's holder offset is still unpinned, so its pointer is not
read directly: it must live in the x19/list windows, identified
there by shape. Every pointer is NULL-guarded; the stub returns
void, writes only the probe buffer, and never suppresses the buy.
Delete after use; never ship.
